#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:123
msgid "data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"START_OG_NEUTRON\"]/text"
msgstr ""
"The arrival beacon lands you in the middle of the Iron Watch's fleet. The fleet pays no attention to you, you observe most ships are preoccupied with preparing for the approaching rebel fleet, engineering ships attend to a number of vessels undergoing repairs.\n"
"\n"
"Your sensors pickup a massive energy signature in the sector, a neutron star, visible even from here. You're unsure how the iron watch have managed to survive with a thing like that around, if you get caught in it's beam it's sure to rip your ship apart."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:132
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"START_OG_NEUTRON\"]/choice[@req=\"og_neutron_dawn_aligned\""
" and @lvl=\"1\"]/text"
msgstr "Continue..."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:136
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"START_OG_NEUTRON\"]/choice[@req=\"og_neutron_dawn_aligned\""
" and @lvl=\"0\"]/text"
msgstr "Continue..."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:141
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_START_IRON\"]/text"
msgstr ""
"You're directed through a series of disinterested officers until you're finally face to face with Admiral Micari, the same Admiral who personally requested your help.\n"
"\n"
"\"Captain, glad you made it, As you may know, I'm Admiral Micari of the 4th Defence Fleet. I'll spare the rest of the formalities and cut right to the chase.\n"
"When I originally requested your assistance, the intention was to have you fight alongside the fleet. The Rebel fleet has already taken out several of our forward outposts, frankly, we could really use another capable ship like yours on the frontline.\""

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:146
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_START_IRON\"]/choice/text"
msgstr "Continue..."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:148
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_START_IRON\"]/choice/event/text"
msgstr ""
"\"That plan has changed, two hours ago we received a distress call coming from our research base, the one positioned right next to the neutron star you may have noticed in the sector. The signal cut out before we could get a clear read on what was happening, it might just be equipment failure, but I fear the worst.\"\n"
"\t\t\t\n"
"\"I can't pull any of my ships from the front line to follow up on the distress signal, not with the Rebel fleet so close. But that research base is part of why we're even here in the first place, I can't disclose details but it's important, and so I can't just ignore the distress call.\""

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:152
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_START_IRON\"]/choice/event/choice/text"
msgstr "Continue..."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:154
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_START_IRON\"]/choice/event/choice/event/text"
msgstr ""
"\"That's where you come in, Captain. I need you to investigate the distress signal and make sure the base is alright. If there is time after that is dealt with, we'd appreciate any help you can provide to the frontline, but that base is the top priority.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Good luck out there Captain.\""

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:158
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_START_IRON\"]/choice/event/choice/event/choice[1]/text"
msgstr "Request support."

