#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:314
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//ship[@name=\"SHIP_OG_DAWN_RESEARCH_FINISHER\"]/destroyed/text"
msgstr ""
"One of the turrets is launched off into empty space as the ship explodes, "
"throwing valuable debris in every direction."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:317
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//ship[@name=\"SHIP_OG_DAWN_RESEARCH_FINISHER\"]/destroyed/choice/text"
msgstr "Continue..."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:322
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//ship[@name=\"SHIP_OG_DAWN_RESEARCH_FINISHER\"]/deadCrew/text"
msgstr ""
"\"You will regret this! Karma always comes back to people like you. Damn you"
" Renegades... the New Dawn will...\" They die before they can finish this "
"last remark."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:326
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//ship[@name=\"SHIP_OG_DAWN_RESEARCH_FINISHER\"]/deadCrew/choice/text"
msgstr "Continue..."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:333
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$/dummyroot/FTL/event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_IRON\"]/text"
msgstr ""
"The research station hangs in orbit above the neutron star, close enough that the radiation in unavoidable, you'll want to avoid spending too long here.\n"
"\n"
"As you bring your ship alongside the station and begin docking procedures, its immediately clear something's gone wrong, the hull of the station is scored with damage, half the solar panels are completely missing."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:337
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$/dummyroot/FTL/event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_IRON\"]/choice/text"
msgstr "Continue..."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:339
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$/dummyroot/FTL/event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_IRON\"]/choice/event/text"
msgstr ""
"The airlock opens into the station, thankfully these part has stayed pressurised despite the damage.\n"
"You're immediately face to face with a figure in the white coat of a scientist. \"You're from the Iron Watch? Close enough, come in quickly.\""

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:342
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$/dummyroot/FTL/event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_IRON\"]/choice/event/choice/text"
msgstr "Continue..."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:344
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$/dummyroot/FTL/event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_IRON\"]/choice/event/choice/event/text"
msgstr ""
"You're ushered towards a nearby meeting room, a large screen is cycling through various images of dangerous looking ship, stealth in design, it must be what attacked the station.\n"
"\n"
"\"We were attacked, that ship,\" they gesture to the one on the screen, \"is unlike anything we've seen before. We've heard stories of 'ghost' ships like this but no one had seriously considered them. We barely saw it coming, it came from the direction of the neutron star, shielded from our sensors by the radiation. They were shielded by one of our own Synchrotron Barriers, developed here on this station to shield our ships against the radiation of the neutron star.\""

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:348
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$/dummyroot/FTL/event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_IRON\"]/choice/event/choice/event/choice/text"
msgstr "Alarms activate throughout the station."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:350
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$/dummyroot/FTL/event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_IRON\"]/choice/event/choice/event/choice/event/text"
msgstr ""
"Alarms blaring across the station, the screen on the wall switches to show a"
" new ship, painted in New Dawn colours. With the station as defenceless as "
"it is, you have the only thing capable of preventing the New Dawn vessel "
"from finishing the station off. You rush back to your ship and disengage "
"from the station, now clear of the station's protection you'll have to "
"survive both the enemy and the force of the radiation."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:353
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$/dummyroot/FTL/event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_IRON\"]/choice/event/choice/event/choice/event/choice/text"
msgstr "Continue..."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:365
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_SAVED\"]/text"
msgstr ""
"You quickly return to the safety of the station's Synchrotron Barrier. Docking with the station, you head back to the meeting room with the scientist, who is now pacing back and forth across the room.\n"
"\n"
"\"That won't be the last of them. The stealth ship, 'ghost' ship as some have been calling it, it wasn't just here to destroy us. No, it was here to steal our stock of Synchrotron Barriers, but worse, they've stolen the schematics, previously they've only been able to get their hands on the devices by stealing them off of our own ships, but now they could begin manufacturing the devices themselves.\""

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:369
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_SAVED\"]/choice/text"
msgstr "Continue..."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:371
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_SAVED\"]/choice/event/text"
msgstr ""
"\"The good news however is that we began placing tracking devices in the barriers, we should be able to track the ones stolen by the 'ghost' ship itself, and if we're quick enough we may be able to prevent the schematics from escaping the sector.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"I'm humbly requesting your help here, we need to recover the schematics. I hope it's not too much to ask, but I'd like to come with you, I assure you I'll be no hindrance onboard the ship.\""

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:375
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_SAVED\"]/choice/event/choice[1]/text"
msgstr "Accept them onboard."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:377
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_SAVED\"]/choice/event/choice[1]/event/text"
msgstr ""
"\"I realise I forgot to introduce myself. Dr. Silas at your service.\"\n"
"\"There's one more thing, this station is done, it's in no condition to be repaired this close to the neutron star. If you can get everyone onboard to safety we can transfer the only Synchrotron Barrier remaining to your ship, the one currently hooked up to the station.\"\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t\n"
"You're able to load the remaining station staff onto your ship, before Dr. Silas has the Synchrotron Barrier carefully moved onto your ship, and integrated into your engines system."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:386
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_SAVED\"]/choice/event/choice[1]/event/choice/text"
msgstr "Continue..."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:388
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_SAVED\"]/choice/event/choice[1]/event/choice/event/text"
msgstr ""
"You're able to deliver the station's staff to a nearby outpost, as you leave"
" you watch the station disintegrate under the full force of the radiation."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:394
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_SAVED\"]/choice/event/choice[2]/text"
msgstr "Refuse the offer."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:396
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_SAVED\"]/choice/event/choice[2]/event/text"
msgstr ""
"\"I will stay with the rest of the station's staff then, good luck with the rest of the mission then, Captain.\"\n"
"\"There's one more thing, this station is done, it's in no condition to be repaired this close to the neutron star. If you can get everyone onboard to safety we can transfer the only Synchrotron Barrier remaining to your ship, the one currently hooked up to the station.\"\n"
"\t\t\t\t\t\n"
"You're able to load the remaining station staff onto your ship, before the scientist has the Synchrotron Barrier carefully moved onto your ship, and integrated into your engines system."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:404
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_SAVED\"]/choice/event/choice[2]/event/choice/text"
msgstr "Continue..."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:406
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_RESEARCH_STATION_SAVED\"]/choice/event/choice[2]/event/choice/event/text"
msgstr ""
"You're able to deliver the station's staff to a nearby outpost, as you leave"
" you watch the station disintegrate under the full force of the radiation."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:426
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_GHOST_IRON_QUEST\"]/beaconType/unvisitedTooltip"
msgstr ""
"The Location of the 'Ghost' ship with the stolen Synchrotron Barriers."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:432
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_GHOST_IRON_QUEST\"]/text"
msgstr ""
"You arrive face to face with 'Ghost' ship, it's even more dangerous looking "
"in person. Sleek and armed to the teeth, this is sure to be a tough fight. "
"You're given no chance to avoid the fight as you're immediately within range"
" of their weapons."

#: src-en/data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml:434
msgid ""
"data/events_sector_og_neutron.xml$//event[@name=\"OG_NEUTRON_GHOST_IRON_QUEST\"]/choice/text"
